take	V;PST;SG;3	took	Rachel Rook took Carroll home to meet her parents two months after she first slept with him.
take	V;PST;SG;3	took	For a generous girl, a girl who took off her clothes with abandon, she was remarkably close-mouthed about some things.
learn	V;PST;V.PTCP	learned	In two months Carroll had learned that her parents lived on a farm several miles outside of town; that they sold strawberries in summer, and Christmas trees in the winter.
know	V;PST;SG;3	knew	He knew that they never left the farm; instead, the world came to them in the shape of weekend picnickers and driveby tourists.
think	V;NFIN	think	Do you think your parents will like me?" he said.
