be	V;PST;SG;3	was	Sometimes there was gunfire outside and we jumped, even Mam on the bed.
wake	V;NFIN	wake	Once Bet was asleep it was impossible to wake her up.
fall	V;PST;SG;1	fell	I fell asleep thinking about how I wished that the Scathalos outrunners were gone.
dream	V;PST;SG;1	dreamed	I dreamed that I was at the offworlder's home, where it was summer but no one was taking care of the stabros, and they were all glad, and so I was a hero - and I was startled awake by gunfire.
wish	V;PST;SG;1	wished	I wished my da would come home.
seem	V;NFIN	seem	It didn't seem fair that we should lie here and be afraid while the men were getting drunk and singing.
illustrate	V;PST;V.PTCP	illustrated	A ROMANCE IN EIGHT DAYS by JOHANN VALENTIN ANDREAE in a new version by JOHN CROWLEY illustrated by THEO FADEL
decide	V;PST;V.PTCP	decided	The Chemical Wedding by Christian Rosencreutz is the way I’ve decided to present the title of this book.
call	V;PST;V.PTCP	called	Most versions in English are called The Chemical Wedding of Christian Rosencreutz, which suggests (and most people who’ve heard of it suppose) that the wedding is Christian’s.
call	V;PST;V.PTCP	called	It’s not; Christian Rosencreutz is the purported author of a book called The Chemical Wedding.
