have	V;PST;SG;3	had	England had better ball possession in the game.
start	V;PST;SG;3	started	England started the match with attacking style, with attempts from Jesse Lingard, Harry Maguire, Harry Kane, and John Stones early in the game.
open	V;PST;SG;3	opened	Then England opened the scoring, when Harry Kane scored a close-ranged shot.
substitute	V;PST;V.PTCP	substituted	Four minutes later, Tunisia's goalkeeper Mouez Hassen was substituted off due to injury and replaced by Farouk Ben Mustapha.
win	V;PST;SG;3	won	Tunisia won a penalty kick in the 33rd minute.
book	V;PST;V.PTCP	booked	English defender Kyle Walker was booked for his bad foul, and Ferjani Sassi scored from the penalty spot, equalising for the African side.
end	V;PST;SG;3	ended	The first half ended 1 – 1 on the scoreboard.
have	V;PST;PL;3	had	In the second half, both sides had attempts for goals, but none crossing the goal line.
score	V;PST;SG;3	scored	In the injury time, English captain Harry Kane scored a second goal as England won a corner kick.
